    "Vanguard Daykeeper HUD": "## VANGUARD DAYKEEPER OPENING\nThe default First Day at Vanguard opens at Term 1, Week 1, Monday 07:30, before FLT-101. Let initialization establish the header. Do not rewrite the institutional calendar from prose. A different authored start may establish a different scene context, but the Academic Ledger remains the calendar owner.",
    "Wardrobe and Personal Spending": "## WARDROBE & PERSONAL SPENDING\nEvery new cadet begins with an equipped Vanguard Standard Softweave Underlayer and a modest 450-credit personal spending balance alongside issued gear. Do not inventory-dump either in the opening. Mention the underlayer only if clothing/changing makes it visible; mention credits when shopping, paying, checking funds or another material choice makes money relevant. Do not assume the PC bought glamorous civilian clothes before play unless their background or starting inventory establishes it.",
    "SpaceFleet — Starting Vessel Handoff": "## SPACEFLEET STARTING VESSEL HANDOFF\nIf the opening begins aboard a mobile spacecraft, establish one specific vessel name when the fiction provides one, plus class/type only when known. Make clear whether the player merely occupies it, owns it, commands it, or belongs to a larger fleet; do not collapse those states. If several players begin on different vessels, establish that split explicitly. Do not invent a ship interior map merely because the start is aboard.",
    "SpaceFleet — Opening Locality and Transit": "If the opening begins aboard a vessel, establish the exact vessel and the player's local subspace without turning the mobile hull into ordinary geography. If the opening begins during transit, distinguish underway travel from arrival and do not silently place the vessel at its destination. Different starting players may be on different hulls/scenes; do not make them co-present unless the start actually says so."
