    "Conversation Starter Guidance": "## SPACEFLEET CONVERSATION STARTERS\n- Open from the NPC's actual role, current vessel/local scene, relationship and immediate business; do not make every crew member announce a system problem or mission hook.\n- Respect locality and communication channels. A remote NPC may open over radio/comms only when a channel is established; an absent NPC does not speak as if physically present.\n- Captains, officers, crew, passengers, dock workers and contacts can begin with practical status, a direct question, an owed answer, routine work, personal conversation or silence as fits the scene.\n- Do not expose registry-private cargo, funds, damage, secret orders or detached-vessel truth beyond what this NPC could actually know.",
