    "relationship_initialization": "\n### relationshipInitialize\nFor each NPC listed as needing relationship initialization, choose an initial relationship score toward the players from -100 to 100 using their background, personality, faction, established history, and current story. Use 0 when neutral is appropriate.\nReturn an absolute score, including the current interaction, rather than a relationshipChange delta.\n",
    "V5.12 Chat and Evidence Continuity": "## CHAT & RELATIONSHIP EVIDENCE\nTreat durable chat facts as evidence only through the channel that actually occurred. Direct promises, refusals, insults, confessions, intimacy, boundary handling and costly support can matter to the involved NPC; hearsay/public reputation is weaker and requires a route. One conversation/outing/lesson/shift is one relationship occasion even if it spans several turns. Do not farm relationship movement per message. Preserve address changes, owed answers and explicit relationship commitments separately from raw score.",
    "SpaceFleet — Vessel Relationship Continuity": "## SPACEFLEET VESSEL CONTINUITY\nPreserve established owner, commanding officer/captain, acting commander, crew affiliation, passenger status, physical-vessel presence, and detached duty unless play actually changes them. Relationship changes do not automatically change command authority, employment, ownership, or fleet membership. If a named crew member transfers vessels, deserts, is captured, dies, goes off-vessel, or returns, keep that status tied to the exact person and exact hull.",
    "SpaceFleet — Evidence and Remote Knowledge": "## SPACEFLEET NPC UPDATE EVIDENCE\n- Do not update an NPC as if they witnessed events on another vessel, compartment, station or planet without a channel. Direct experience, live comms/sensor feed, later report and hearsay are different evidence.\n- Remote orders, warnings, promises and reports may change knowledge or relationship only to the extent actually communicated. Hidden registry events cause no social update until discovered.\n- Command, ownership, party membership and physical presence remain separate; do not infer one from another."
