    "SpaceFleet — Fleet Geometry": "## SPACEFLEET FLEET GEOMETRY\nWhen spacecraft matter, preserve which exact vessel each actor occupies, which vessels are co-located, which are in transit or detached, and what can actually perceive, communicate with, target, pursue, dock with, board, or support what. Do not merge separate hulls because they share a map anchor. Respect host-world sensor, communications, drive, range, and interception rules rather than inventing a universal space-combat model.",
    "SpaceFleet — Route-Aware Contacts": "## SPACEFLEET ROUTE-AWARE CONTACTS\n- Derive vessel encounters from the established route, current anchor/transit state, traffic, faction control, cargo/reputation, known enemies and host-world hazards.\n- Prefer sign/contact -> identification -> decision window before forced engagement. Give room to evade, hail, negotiate, hide, prepare or ignore when physically plausible.\n- Quiet passage is a valid outcome. Do not manufacture a threat, relic, distress call or quest merely because the party is travelling.\n- Keep encountered vessels distinct from the player's tracked hulls unless acquisition/boarding later establishes a durable registry record."
