  "ItemGenerationAndUsage": {
    "SpaceFleet — Hull Property and Refits": "## SPACEFLEET VESSEL PROPERTY\nInstalled spacecraft systems, permanent refits, carried cargo, loose equipment, and lasting damage belong to the exact physical vessel that owns or carries them. Do not silently copy upgrades between ships of the same class. Loose personal items remain character inventory unless actually installed or transferred. Host-world technology decides compatibility; this mod supplies persistence, not a universal tech tree.",
    "custom": "## ITEM INSTRUCTIONS\n\n## NEVER Update For\n- Items merely seen, discussed, offered, displayed, inspected, or nearby\n- Storage or reorganization (putting items in bags, packs, pouches, pockets) -- NEVER a remove\n- Other characters' actions on their own inventory\n- Trades or transfers between NPCs\n- Unconfirmed offers, quotes, negotiations, or stated prices without player agreement\n\n## Non-Combat Item Changes\n\nADD only when an item physically enters the player's possession -- taken, picked up, received, looted, handed to them, or crafted by them.\nREMOVE only when an item physically leaves the player's possession -- handed over, expended, consumed, discarded, destroyed, or taken from them.\n\nSearching or looting a body, container, or location implies taking found items unless the player explicitly states otherwise.\n\nCompleted transactions are TWO-WAY: if currency is removed for a purchase, the received goods MUST be added. If goods are handed over, payment MUST be added.\n\nTRANSACTION TIMING: A transaction requires BOTH a stated price AND the player explicitly paying or agreeing AFTER the price is stated. \"I'll take it\" before a price is quoted is NOT confirmation. \nAn NPC placing items on a counter is NOT a completed transaction. Only update when the player actually hands over currency or confirms the final price.\n\nQuantities must match what actually changed. Do not add or remove an entire stack unless the story clearly shows the full stack changed hands or was consumed.\n\nPerform the update immediately once actual change of hands occurs.\n\n## Combat Item Rules\n\nConsumables (potions, scrolls, arrows, thrown weapons) are removed when used in combat.\n\nEQUIPMENT DURABILITY: Normal combat does NOT damage or destroy equipped weapons or armor. Hits, blocks, parries, clashes, and impacts are expected wear. Vivid combat narration -- sparks flying, dents forming, leather scoring -- is dramatic flavor, NOT mechanical damage. Do not interpret combat descriptions as equipment destruction.\n\nEquipment damage ONLY occurs from EXTRAORDINARY events:\n- A targeted attack explicitly intended to destroy the specific item\n- Environmental destruction (acid, lava, disintegration magic)\n- Powerful magic specifically described as shattering or unmaking gear\n- The player deliberately sacrificing or abandoning an item\n- Explicit narrative statement that the item is broken beyond use\n\nIf an extraordinary event occurs: remove the original and add a \"Damaged [Item Name]\" version, equipping it automatically. A \"Damaged\" item still functions and is only destroyed if ANOTHER extraordinary event specifically targets it. Normal combat does NOT destroy \"Damaged\" items.\nWhen uncertain, preserve the item.\n\n\n## Before Output, Confirm:\n\n1. Did items physically change possession? If not, output nothing.\n2. Does any entry match the NEVER list? If yes, remove it.\n3. For purchases: did the player confirm AFTER a price was stated?\n4. Am I removing equipped gear? Was there an extraordinary destruction event? If just normal combat, preserve the item."
  },
  "summarization": {
    "Vanguard Daykeeper State": "## VANGUARD DAYKEEPER STATE\nExact clock minutes, Term/Week/day, class block, HUD visibility and war alert are trigger-owned state and normally should not be duplicated in prose summaries. Preserve durable consequences caused by time: missed classes, completed qualifications, instructor deployment, appointments kept or missed, leave consumed, mission deadlines and lasting schedule changes. Do not turn temporary HUD labels into permanent lore.",
    "Wardrobe and Purchase Continuity": "## WARDROBE & PURCHASE CONTINUITY\nPreserve consequential clothing facts only when forgetting them would contradict play: a newly purchased signature outfit or lingerie set, what is currently equipped during an unfinished changing/private/formal scene, borrowed/lost/damaged clothing, a meaningful gifted garment, or an exact credit expenditure/debt that still matters. Do not summarize routine underwear every day. A purchased item remains personal property; a tried-on item does not. Underwear remains a separate equipped layer from outer clothing.",
    "V5.12 NPC Chat Continuity": "## NPC CHAT CONTINUITY\nWhen a chat creates durable facts, preserve the precise change: promise, debt, order, price, item loan/gift, invitation, refusal, apology, insult, threat, confession, lie, corrected fact, secret revealed, medical restriction, relationship/sexual boundary, accepted romantic commitment, changed form of address, or an answer/task still owed. Preserve who knows it and how they learned it. Do not summarize mere friendly tone as a new relationship state, and do not make private disclosures public without a channel.",
    "SpaceFleet — Fleet Memory": "## SPACEFLEET FLEET MEMORY\nPreserve exact vessel continuity across summaries: registry identity/#, current and former names, class/type if known, owner, commanding officer/captain, acting commander, fleet commander, fleet membership, each player’s current vessel, last confirmed position, transit state/destination, installed systems, lasting damage, crew condition, important named crew/passengers, cargo/economy facts that matter, detached mission orders/waypoints/rendezvous, and whether information is confirmed or merely expected. Never collapse two similarly named vessels.",
    "SpaceFleet — Carried Craft and Knowledge": "## SPACEFLEET CARRIED CRAFT & KNOWLEDGE\nPreserve parent/child docking relationships, berth state, fleet formation/lead/ROE/rally/escort/standing orders, and the distinction between actual registry state and player last-confirmed knowledge for detached vessels.",
    "SpaceFleet — Channels, Uncertainty and Travel": "## SPACEFLEET SUMMARY DISCIPLINE\n- Preserve per-player vessel/local-scene separation, established communication channels, transit state, destination/route, carried-craft parent/berth state, and fleet orders that remain active.\n- For detached or out-of-contact vessels, preserve last-confirmed information and uncertainty rather than converting hidden registry truth into player knowledge.\n- Preserve exact vessel identity by registry/hull number when names collide or a hull has been renamed."
